menuconfig USING_TEST_FWK
    bool "On-device unit test framework (Unity) glue"
    default n
    help
        Enable the on-device glue around the vendored Unity 2.7.0 C unit
        test framework: the Unity output configuration (unity_config.h) and
        the suite registry/runner that exports the msh commands unity_run
        and unity_list.

        A test project also needs RT_USING_UNITY for the framework itself.
        Production firmware should leave both off; this is meant for the
        projects under example/test/.

config TEST_FWK_AUTORUN
    bool "Run every registered Unity case once at boot"
    default n
    depends on USING_TEST_FWK
    help
        Have a test project call sifli_unity_autorun() from main(), so a
        flashed board runs every suite before anyone could have sent a
        command, and the host only has to read.

        There is no reliable moment to send one instead: unity_run only works
        once the shell is up, and nothing announces that dependably. A command
        that lands early is simply lost, and the run then reports a missing
        Unity summary, which reads as a firmware fault.

        The shell is unaffected: main() still falls through to its loop, so
        unity_run keeps working for hands-on work. Set this to n in proj.conf
        to get a board that waits for a command instead.
